/ An explicit null is a real, typed, present value (Type "null") occupying the variable — it is
/ NOT the same as a never-set variable (which resolves to not-found; WhereUnsetVariableIsNotFound
/ pins that side). Here we pin the value side: assigning null yields a present null-typed value
/ that reads back as null.
ExplicitNullIsAPresentNullValue
- set %x% = null
- assert %x!type.name% equals "null"
- assert %x% is null
